case: malformed dispatch (delegate_task)
gate: plugins/dispatch-envelope-gate/gate.py validate_dispatch
input: tasks[1] = {'goal': 'placeholder'}
block action: block
block message:
  Dispatch blocked: repair every listed task, then resend.
  #1 goal="placeholder" — goal: supply at least 15 non-whitespace characters; goal: replace placeholder text with the real deliverable; option: supply exactly one route: coder, gemini-app, researcher, reviewer, verifier, writer, writer-internal; brief.TASK: add a line beginning 'TASK:' with its value; brief.FACTS: add a line beginning 'FACTS:' with its value; brief.PATHS: add a line beginning 'PATHS:' with its value; brief.OUTPUT: add a line beginning 'OUTPUT:' with its value; brief.CHECK: add a line beginning 'CHECK:' with its value; brief.CEILING: add a line beginning 'CEILING:' with its value
  
  Copy this six-line envelope into each task's goal (or its context) and fill it in:
  goal is emitted on every call and is the field that always arrives; context is optional and some models omit it.
  TASK: <deliverable>
  FACTS: <facts, none, or self-contained>
  PATHS: <exact file paths/URLs or n/a>
  OUTPUT: <what the return must contain>
  CHECK: <acceptance check>
  CEILING: <max turns, include a number>
verdict: CAUGHT
